pg_procstat
===========

This module provides test functions for procstat file operations.

Functions
---------

qdb_procstat_test_write(value integer) - void
  Writes an integer value to a test file in the PostgreSQL data directory.
  The file is named 'pg_procstat_test.dat' and is created in the data
  directory. If the file exists, it will be overwritten.

qdb_procstat_test_read() - integer
  Reads an integer value from the test file created by qdb_procstat_test_write().
  Returns the integer value stored in the file.
  Raises an error if the file doesn't exist or cannot be read.

Usage Example
-------------

After installing the extension:

  CREATE EXTENSION pg_procstat;

  -- Write a value to the test file
  SELECT qdb_procstat_test_write(42);

  -- Read the value back
  SELECT qdb_procstat_test_read();  -- Returns: 42

Notes
-----

The test file is stored in the PostgreSQL data directory and persists
across sessions. The file operations use PostgreSQL's transient file
API for proper resource management.
